    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">2021-2022 Targets:

Output 1: Community-based conflict resolution and reconciliation mechanisms (CBRMs) are in use and working effectively to resolve conflict.
&#x2022; All members of the 10 newly established Community Based Resolution Mechanism (CBRM) members will be trained on the different skills and knowledge on local conflict prevention and resolution techniques.
&#x2022; 10 communities will be reached and supported by CBRM
&#x2022; Produce information Educational and Communicational materials on conflict prevention and peace building.

Output 2: Peace dividends for community interdependence and coexistence delivered.
&#x2022; Select and train 10 women group (each 25 members) on Saving for Change (SfC) model.
&#x2022; Select 10 women &amp;10 Youth groups (15 each) to receive cash grants to establish small income
&#x2022; Rehabilitate Hafirs and 10 hand pumps that are used by different tribes in the targeted 10villages.

Output 3: Improved networking, coordination and learning between local and state-level peacebuilding institutions.
&#x2022; Existing CBOs will be strengthened and trained in 10 villages to support the role of CBRM and formation of peace building networks.
&#x2022; Build local actors capacities in conflict prevention, mitigation and peace-building through formation and strengthening of peace committees with fair representation of all stakeholders (IDPs, returnees, women, youth, farmers, pastoralists and traditional leaders).
&#x2022; Establishing dialogue among conflicting groups, promoting peaceful coexistence and increasing the level of trust, confidence and peace building among sedentary farmers and pastoralists.
&#x2022; Provide a range of livelihoods options and asset, support youth and women groups through skills training with particular focus on marketable skill that will help to establish small business, natural resource management, animal restocking for poor households, provision of small business startup packages, and distribution of donkey carts.
&#x2022; Ensure increased and equitable access to water for human and animals through construction and/or rehabilitating of water sources (Hafir and hand pumps).</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022; 10 CBRMs established (number of members to be clarified). 
&#x2022; Completed selection for Saving for Change (SfC) groups. 4 (100 F) out of 10 women group members have been trained SfC model.
&#x2022; Completed selection of beneficiaries for Income Generating Activities/IGAs activities, 4 (100 F) out of 10 women groups members have been trained on Income generating activities (IGAs).
&#x2022; Completed selection the sites for Open hand dug well and hand pumps rehabilitation.
&#x2022; The tender process and supervision by KSCS civil engineer construction of the hand dug well is going on. In this reporting period two retch water.
&#x2022; Tender process and supervision by KSCS civil engineer rehabilitation of the hand pump is going on. In this reporting period three hand pumps were rehabilitated as well.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
